cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  IMPORTANT: Citation metadata is incomplete. Complete the authors, release
  version, archive DOI, release date, rights holder, and license before public
  release or citation.
title: "E2N: An Auditable Protein-to-Nanomaterial Translation Framework for Dual-Target Nanozyme Hypotheses"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "REQUIRED BEFORE PUBLIC RELEASE: replace with the complete contribution-ordered author list"
repository-code: "https://github.com/taxuannga877-jpg/enzyme-to-nanozyme"
url: "https://github.com/taxuannga877-jpg/enzyme-to-nanozyme"
abstract: >-
  E2N is an auditable computational framework and paper-facing release for
  translating selected metalloenzyme evidence into explicit, topology-aware
  nanomaterial hypotheses. The canonical x1-x100 snapshot contains 355
  retained canonical candidate records, 699 complete activity-specific
  profiles, and 3515 converged frames within complete profiles. These records
  support release-level figure, statistical, and report reproduction; they do
  not constitute experimental catalyst validation or a full upstream campaign
  rebuild.
keywords:
  - nanozyme
  - metalloenzyme
  - computational materials design
  - scientific reproducibility
  - evidence provenance
version: "REQUIRED BEFORE PUBLIC RELEASE"

